# =============================================================================
# AutoJob Agent - Cron Job Configuration Example
# =============================================================================
#
# CRON_MODE is a hard safety boundary that ensures scheduled runs:
# - Only discover jobs from public APIs
# - Only extract emails from public career pages
# - NEVER invoke LLMs
# - NEVER generate resumes
# - NEVER draft emails
# - NEVER send emails
#
# IMPORTANT: Always set CRON_MODE=true for scheduled runs.
#
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# OPTION A: Discover-only (read-only, no LLM, no emails)
# =============================================================================
# Run job discovery every 6 hours
# This scrapes RemoteOK and HackerNews for new AI/ML job listings
0 */6 * * * CRON_MODE=true /path/to/python -m app.main discover >> /var/log/autojob/discover.log 2>&1

# Alternative: Run discovery at specific times (9am, 3pm, 9pm)
# 0 9,15,21 * * * CRON_MODE=true /path/to/python -m app.main discover >> /var/log/autojob/discover.log 2>&1

# =============================================================================
# OPTION B: Full pipeline (discover + resume + email draft, NO sending)
# =============================================================================
# Discovers jobs, generates tailored resumes and email drafts for each.
# Jobs land in PENDING state — you manually approve and send later.
# NOTE: Do NOT set CRON_MODE=true here — it would block LLM/resume generation.
#
# Run full pipeline every Monday at 9 AM
0 9 * * 1 cd /path/to/auto-job && /path/to/python -m app.main run-all >> /var/log/autojob/run_all.log 2>&1

# =============================================================================
# IMPORTANT NOTES
# =============================================================================
#
# 1. ALWAYS include CRON_MODE=true
#    Without this flag, the system may attempt LLM calls or email sending.
#
# 2. Only use 'discover' command in cron jobs
#    The following commands are allowed in CRON_MODE:
#    - discover: Scrape jobs and extract emails
#    - list: View discovered jobs (read-only)
#    - status: View system status (read-only)
#
#    The following commands are BLOCKED in CRON_MODE:
#    - process: Would attempt LLM calls
#    - approve/reject: Approval flow is blocked
#    - (any future LLM-related commands)
#
# 3. Check logs for CRON_MODE confirmation
#    Logs should show: "CRON_MODE active - blocking LLM operations"
#
# 4. Test your cron setup
#    Run manually first: CRON_MODE=true python -m app.main discover
#    Verify: No LLM API calls, no emails sent, jobs.json updated
#
# =============================================================================
# WINDOWS TASK SCHEDULER EQUIVALENT
# =============================================================================
#
# For Windows, use Task Scheduler with:
# Program: cmd.exe
# Arguments: /c "set CRON_MODE=true && cd C:\path\to\job-agent && python -m app.main discover"
# Schedule: Every 6 hours
#
# Or use PowerShell:
# Program: powershell.exe
# Arguments: -Command "$env:CRON_MODE='true'; cd 'C:\path\to\job-agent'; python -m app.main discover"
#
# =============================================================================
